  "error_schema": {},
  "gotchas": [
    "The API key comes from the developers tab of your account on voice.intron.io; send it as 'Authorization: Bearer {key}' from your backend only — the docs say never expose it in client-side code.",
    "Poll until processing_status is FILE_TRANSCRIBED (results present) or FILE_PROCESSING_FAILED. The other values are FILE_QUEUED, FILE_PENDING and FILE_PROCESSING; the in-progress example shows only processing_status and audio_file_name in data.",
    "get_structured_post_processing takes 'f' or 't' (default 'f' = Markdown text). Every documented example is the default text form; the JSON shape returned with 't' is not documented, so transcript_* fields may not be strings then.",
    "The documented status responses do not echo file_id — keep it on your side.",
    "get_icd_codes output has two names in the docs: transcript_icd_codes in the procedure examples, transcript_billing_codes in the completed example on Get File Status. Read both.",
    "No dedicated response field is documented for get_differential_diagnosis, get_followup_instructions or get_practice_guidelines: in the completed example on Get File Status their output appears as sections inside transcript_suggestions.",
    "The documented examples return status \"Ok\" and message \"file status found\". No error response is documented for this endpoint (unknown file_id, invalid key, rate limit).",
    "Rate limit: 100 requests per minute on status. Responses carry rate-limit headers; Retry-After gives the delay in seconds before retrying."
  ],
